body:
Split from #583 by ADR-0010. This is valuable platform/security hardening but is not a fast-path causal-identification or physical-start prerequisite.

## Prerequisite consumed from #583

The fast v2 study does **not** defer its minimum integrity boundary. #583 must first deliver five distinct P0 duties with bounded functions/grants and allow/deny tests:

1. restricted randomizer with internal secret use and no pre-reveal raw-secret read;
2. lifecycle controller for legal v2 state transitions only;
3. component executor using only the phase-appropriate least-information readiness, randomized or recovery-only resolver;
4. outcome freezer may read blinded assignment ID/X-Y label/phase lineage to produce immutable exports, but cannot mutate assignments or read A/B mapping/secret; and
5. a separate blinded analyst with read-only access to frozen X/Y exports until reveal.

The experiment cannot claim integrity if a shared owner can rewrite schedule/mapping/outcomes. Any concrete minimum needed to enforce that invariant belongs in #583/#639/#640 and remains a #642 gate.

## Deferred platform-wide scope

After the minimum above exists, replace shared schema-owner credentials across all experiment-adjacent workloads with explicit least-privilege roles and bounded mutation functions:

- migration owner, usable only by the ledgered PreSync migration path;
- API lifecycle role beyond the study-minimum surface;
- ingestor/component executor and future vector-arbiter roles;
- planner/context read-only role;
- MCP proposal-only role;
- analyst/blinded-export roles across general workloads;
- twin read-only role;
- any non-authoritative `planner_graph` role retained in desired state.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Grants/revokes ship through new ledgered migrations; applied migrations are never edited.
- [ ] Every workload references a distinct bounded credential delivered through the authorized secret mechanism. No secret value or Secret annotation is printed, copied or committed.
- [ ] A live-role allow/deny matrix proves intended functions and rejects direct table DML, mapping reads and cross-surface access.
- [ ] Owner/migration credentials are absent from normal workload pods.
- [ ] Rotation and rollback are rehearsed without downtime or loss of the single-writer fence.
- [ ] Public/API/planner health, migrations and experiment feature-off behavior remain unchanged.
- [ ] #583's minimum five-role P0 contract remains intact; this broader work neither weakens nor retroactively gates the fast launch.

## Boundary

This P2 issue defers only repository/platform-wide credential separation and future-workload hardening. It does not own the v2 randomization/result ledger, readiness/randomized/recovery-only resolvers, append-only experiment mutations or freezer/analyst separation required by #583/#639/#640.
